@trait {
  name: "@transaction",
  category: "economics",
  description: "On-chain transaction authoring and lifecycle tracking for HoloScript entities. chain selects the target L1/L2 network: ethereum, polygon, base, or arbitrum. signer_type controls the key-management surface: wallet (external EOA signer such as MetaMask / WalletConnect), passkey (WebAuthn credential bound to the device), or session_key (a short-lived delegated key issued by the seat wallet for gas-free or subsidised flows). gas_limit sets the EVM execution gas ceiling; 0 = estimate. max_fee_gwei caps the EIP-1559 maxFeePerGas in gwei; 0 = market. simulate bool enables a dry-run through the chain's eth_call / debug_traceCall surface before broadcasting — useful for catching reverts without spending gas. Emits on_pending when the transaction is broadcast and waiting for inclusion, on_confirmed when the receipt lands with a non-zero status, on_failed when the transaction reverts or is dropped, and on_receipt with the full decoded receipt object. Pairs with @economy_primitives for currency/price-oracle coordination and @wallet for signer resolution. Research: TransactionTrait.ts — TransactionConfig, TxReceipt, debitBalance / stakeBalance / depositBalance flows. CANONICAL @transaction: this is the sole file declaring the bare '@transaction' name (task_1784182188049_7xzd, 2026-07-16 disambiguation — see core_transaction.holo and atomic_transaction.holo, which previously duplicated this name and are now @core_transaction / @atomic_transaction respectively). If you need the local wallet-ledger trait (pay/transfer/stake/unstake/deposit, no chain broadcast), use @core_transaction, the native description of the shipped packages/core/src/traits/TransactionTrait.ts handler.",
  props: {
    chain: enum("ethereum" | "polygon" | "base" | "arbitrum") = "base",
    signer_type: enum("wallet" | "passkey" | "session_key") = "wallet",
    gas_limit: number = 0,
    max_fee_gwei: number = 0,
    simulate: boolean = false
  },
  events: {
    attached: "transaction:attached",
    detached: "transaction:detached",
    on_pending: "transaction:pending",
    on_confirmed: "transaction:confirmed",
    on_failed: "transaction:failed",
    on_receipt: "transaction:receipt",
    on_error: "transaction:error",
    on_send: "transaction:send",
    on_cancel: "transaction:cancel",
    on_query_ledger: "transaction:query_ledger"
  },
  behaviors: ["@economy_primitives", "@wallet"]
}
